# Source: https://github.com/kundajelab/atac_dnase_pipelines/issues/41
# Symptom: BED mixes chr-prefixed standard chromosomes (chr1, chr2) with
#   unlocalized scaffold names that lack the chr prefix (GL000008.2,
#   KI270728.1); bedtools reports "inconsistent naming convention" because
#   it detects a mix of named styles in the same file.  Arises from merging
#   alignments from hg38 where scaffold contigs are named without chr prefix
#   while standard chromosomes keep it.  Downstream intersect operations
#   silently drop reads on scaffolds.
chr1	100	200	read001	1000	+
chr2	50000	50100	read002	1000	-
GL000008.2	41	88	read003	1000	+
KI270728.1	200	350	read004	1000	-
chr3	1000	1100	read005	999	+
